# Code Quality and Standards Rules

## 🔍 Code Quality Standards

### TypeScript Rules

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Proper TypeScript usage
interface UserProps {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  isActive?: boolean;
}

function UserProfile({ id, name, email, isActive = false }: UserProps) {
  // Component logic
}

// ❌ WRONG - Using any type
function UserProfile(props: any) {
  // Component logic
}
```

### MUST FOLLOW Rules

✅ **ALWAYS** use strict TypeScript with proper interfaces
✅ **ALWAYS** use path aliases (@components, @utils, etc.)
✅ **ALWAYS** follow ESLint and Prettier configurations
✅ **ALWAYS** use proper naming conventions
✅ **ALWAYS** handle all possible states (loading, error, success)
✅ **ALWAYS** implement proper error boundaries
✅ **ALWAYS** use React.memo for expensive components
✅ **ALWAYS** implement proper accessibility features

### NEVER DO Rules

❌ **NEVER** use `any` type - create proper interfaces
❌ **NEVER** ignore TypeScript errors
❌ **NEVER** use relative imports when path aliases exist
❌ **NEVER** forget to handle edge cases
❌ **NEVER** create components without proper error handling
❌ **NEVER** use console.log in production code
❌ **NEVER** forget to add proper JSDoc comments for complex functions

### ESLint Configuration

```json
{
  "extends": [
    "airbnb-base",
    "plugin:jsx-a11y/recommended",
    "plugin:import/errors",
